VALUES ('neetug-bio-520571', 520571, 'NEET-UG', 'Biology', 'plant-respiration', 'plant-respiration', 'NCERT Biology Class 11, Chapter 12', 'The main way of ATP production in the body is', 'oxidative phosphorylation', 'substrate-level phosphorylation', 'citric acid cycle', 'phosphocreatine breakdown', 'A', 'Oxidative phosphorylation is the primary method of ATP production in most cells. Substrate-level phosphorylation occurs directly within metabolic pathways, while the citric acid cycle generates intermediates used for energy but not ATP directly. Phosphocreatine breakdown provides a rapid source of phosphate groups but is not the main way of ATP production.', 100, 90, 'approved', true)
